 in game  before the living avengers pull their  time travel plan completely together  tony uses david dutch's model of quantum  mechanics  and sent this message to bruce banner  altering events of the past  could never affect the continuous loop  though  it could create tangential split  timelines  let's not worry about that for the time  being right  question mark one reality at a time for  all our sanity  now this is very very big news because  it shows that tony stark  knew the consequences and the risk of  time travel creating alternate timelines  tony stark is one of the smartest people  in the marvel cinematic universe on  earth  and he was clearly thinking about every  single possible scenario of what they  were going to do with their so-called  time heist  and of course he came to the conclusion  that what they were about to do  could affect the other universes  creating different timelines and  alternate realities this  is even more apparent that tony stark  knew this when you look at the scene  with him and captain america right after  thanos attacks the avengers compound and  tony gives captain back his shield he  tells captain america  you mess with time it tends to mess back  now a lot of people have been wondering  what is this specifically referring to  and while of course it is immediately  referring to thanos there is a lot more  to it than that  as with most time travel movies there  are consequences to going back in time  and altering it  but all of those movies don't exist  within a larger universe where all of  the films are interconnected  avengers in-game however exists in the  mcu  where one thing affects everything and  we 100 know that avengers in game did  create  alternate timelines and other universes  and this is where time starts to mess  back the avengers went back in multiple  points in time  and although some timelines may have  been cleared up by captain america  returning the infinity stones  there were still other timelines created  loki created one when he escaped with  the tesseract which of course  is the space stone and he'll probably  hop around into other universes as well  2014's timeline was changed and a  different one created when thanos from  2014 came to the present time and of  course no doubt we'll learn about more  created  but now what we have is a bunch of  different universes with different  paths but the avengers and other  characters the same ones from our  universe  now exist in other universes going down  different paths and as i mentioned  before this leads to two things  kang and avengers secret wars battle  world  kang is the master of time the time  travel king and it's pretty much all but  confirmed that he's going to be  appearing in ant-man 3.  and it's widely assumed that jonathan  majors is going to be playing kang  since he's been cast for a role in the  movie now through the comics king has  traveled through  various different timelines conquering  them all hence his name kang the  conqueror  and now the avengers have messed with  and altered other timelines  and this is bad news for our heroes  because kang the conqueror the master of  time travel probably doesn't like people  messing with his timelines  and not to mention he probably doesn't  like other people figuring out time  travel as well  as most villains want everything to  themselves kang is probably no exception  and much like in the comics kang will  most likely want to destroy  the avengers and of course the fantastic  four once they enter the mcu  but this is why king the conqueror is  going to be one of the next big bad  villains of the mcu  but ultimately all of this is going to  come full  circle from avengers and game to  avengers secret wars  throughout marvel's phase 4 marvel's  phase 5 and marvel's phase 6  we are going to see the repercussions of  the avengers going back in time and  changing some events of the past and  creating alternate universes  the mcu will explore this in many  